# ================================================================================
MOST LIKELY CAUSE

The original code has this flow:

1. PAI calls submit_request
1. submit_request calls builder->submit_request
1. builder->submit_request calls save_request (sets DRAFT)
1. Then tries to UPDATE to PENDING
1. Then triggers workflow

PROBLEM: The UPDATE happens in the same database LUW (Logical Unit of Work)
and might not be committed before workflow trigger.

FIX: Add explicit “COMMIT WORK AND WAIT” after the status update,
BEFORE calling trigger_workflow.

This ensures the database record has status = ‘PENDING’ before workflow starts.

